465:On the whole line the factor is a frequency-domain formula and the policy is a \emph{filter}, a transfer function that maps the observed signal to the position; the classical portfolio and execution rules are its special cases --- Markowitz when the friction is constant, the aim portfolio when it is a second-order differential operator, the moving-average filters of the resilience models, and a fractional derivative when the impact is scale-free. The shape of the policy is set by the impact memory: a rational kernel has finitely many relaxation rates and the position is a finite sum of moving averages; a power-law kernel has a continuum and the policy is a fractional derivative, keeping a fraction $\sin(\pi\beta/2)$ of the value a clairvoyant trader would earn.
